libthe-seed 0.5.0

* DependencyLister now credits every input program with every library it
  needs, directly or through other libraries. Before, a library reached by
  several programs was credited only to the first one that reached it, so the
  result depended on the order of the inputs.

  Packaging output for existing projects can grow: more libraries are now
  attributed to the programs that need them, including libraries that were
  previously missing from every program but the first, and delay-loaded Windows
  libraries. This is the intended correction. Check bundle contents and sizes
  after upgrading.

* Delay-loaded libraries of Windows programs (the delay-load import table) are
  now listed. A malformed delay-load table is rejected like any other
  malformed PE structure.

* New field DependencyResult::libraryErrors (additive; a caller that ignores
  it sees the same keys and errors as before). A library that was found but
  cannot be read is still listed in `dependencies`, and is now reported here
  with the reason and the sorted list of inputs that need it. `errors` still
  holds only inputs named in the request.

* The lists in `dependencies` are now sorted. Libraries are keyed by the real
  file's canonical path, or by the recorded name when not found. PE library
  names match without regard to letter case; ELF names match exactly. Names
  containing a folder separator, "..", a drive prefix or a NUL are not joined
  to a search folder; they are listed under the recorded name.

* Mach-O inputs are declined: the input appears in `errors` with
  "<path>: Mach-O files are not supported for dependency listing" (a Mach-O
  library gets the same text in `libraryErrors`). This will be revisited after
  roadmap task 5. MachOParser::ListDependencies now reads weak, re-exported,
  lazy and upward references, reads every slice of a universal file and
  rejects an unterminated library name.

* Version 0.5.0 (was 0.4.1). The libtool library version is unchanged.
